# Abstract length (hard requirement)

The manuscript abstract must be **1920 characters or fewer**. This is an arXiv hard limit, not a preference. Do not finish an abstract edit that exceeds it.

- Count the collapsed abstract body (whitespace squeezed to single spaces), **including TeX commands**, from `\begin{abstract}` to `\end{abstract}`
- The abstract must contain no custom macros (`abstract-macros.mdc`); count the text as written
- After any abstract change, count and trim before compiling or committing
- Cut Gaia, asides, and duplicated survey detail first; keep the SHS definition, the two developments, and the Euclid/Roman search yields
